 ## Overview
-This article defines the composite training loss functions used in two distinct but related approaches to optimizing neural representations for volume rendering and compression. The first approach [S1] optimizes a physics-based material model and Signed Distance Function (SDF) for inverse rendering, balancing image reconstruction with geometric priors. The second approach [S2] optimizes compressed 3D embeddings for Instant-NGP-based NeRFs, integrating an entropy-based rate distortion term to control bitrate during training.
+This article defines the composite training loss functions used in two distinct but related approaches to optimizing neural representations for volume rendering and compression [S1, S2]. The first approach [S1] optimizes a physics-based material model and Signed Distance Function (SDF) for inverse rendering, balancing image reconstruction with geometric priors. The second approach [S2] optimizes compressed 3D embeddings for Instant-NGP-based NeRFs, integrating an entropy-based rate distortion term to control bitrate during training.
 
